WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.352 --> 00:00:03.390
(emotional music)

00:00:03.390 --> 00:00:07.493
- What you really want to
see is Black Wall Street.

00:00:08.520 --> 00:00:11.910
You want to see the Greenwood District

00:00:11.910 --> 00:00:14.820
thriving with hundreds
of Black-owned businesses

00:00:14.820 --> 00:00:17.010
lining the streets of Greenwood.

00:00:17.010 --> 00:00:18.700
However, much of the property today

00:00:18.700 --> 00:00:21.433
does not belong to African Americans.

00:00:22.330 --> 00:00:23.670
- It's a gift to be able to say

00:00:23.670 --> 00:00:25.750
you come from such amazing people,

00:00:25.750 --> 00:00:29.260
and that you're on the
grounds of what used to be

00:00:29.260 --> 00:00:32.068
something the world had never seen before.

00:00:32.068 --> 00:00:35.000
I've always felt a connection
to Black Wall Street

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:35.963
and to rebirth it.

00:00:37.930 --> 00:00:39.890
- [Narrator] The Tulsa Massacre of 1921

00:00:39.890 --> 00:00:41.840
destroyed nearly 200 businesses

00:00:41.840 --> 00:00:45.370
in the area that came to be
known as Black Wall Street.

00:00:45.370 --> 00:00:47.210
Now, entrepreneurs and activists

00:00:47.210 --> 00:00:49.520
are pushing to carry on its legacy.

00:00:49.520 --> 00:00:51.660
They're advocating for
more Black-owned businesses

00:00:51.660 --> 00:00:54.010
and property ownership,
amid gentrification

00:00:54.010 --> 00:00:56.593
that's reshaping the
historic Black neighborhood.

00:00:58.700 --> 00:01:01.240
The Greenwood district of Tulsa, Oklahoma

00:01:01.240 --> 00:01:02.870
was once a center of Black wealth

00:01:02.870 --> 00:01:05.240
in the early 20th century.

00:01:05.240 --> 00:01:06.810
Located north of railroad tracks

00:01:06.810 --> 00:01:09.110
that divided Tulsa during segregation,

00:01:09.110 --> 00:01:10.270
it was home to thousands

00:01:10.270 --> 00:01:12.343
of Black Tulsans and their businesses.

00:01:13.350 --> 00:01:16.600
But 1921, white mobs attacked the district

00:01:16.600 --> 00:01:18.400
killing dozens of Black residents

00:01:18.400 --> 00:01:20.560
and destroying about 35 square blocks

00:01:20.560 --> 00:01:22.560
over the course of one night.

00:01:22.560 --> 00:01:26.260
Researchers say the damages
filed in court cases decades ago

00:01:26.260 --> 00:01:29.980
total over 22 million in today's dollars.

00:01:29.980 --> 00:01:32.670
But this likely underestimates
the actual losses,

00:01:32.670 --> 00:01:34.850
as not everyone had
full insurance coverage,

00:01:34.850 --> 00:01:36.530
or went to court.

00:01:36.530 --> 00:01:38.670
After the massacre, Black entrepreneurs

00:01:38.670 --> 00:01:40.780
worked to rebuild Greenwood.

00:01:40.780 --> 00:01:43.930
But local historians say the
district went through a decline

00:01:43.930 --> 00:01:46.570
as desegregation led to outward migration,

00:01:46.570 --> 00:01:48.330
and urban renewal programs

00:01:48.330 --> 00:01:51.283
displaced Black-owned
businesses and residents.

00:01:52.750 --> 00:01:56.480
Today, Greenwood consists
of about four city blocks.

00:01:56.480 --> 00:01:58.680
There's not much housing
stock in the neighborhood,

00:01:58.680 --> 00:02:00.530
and just over two dozen Black-owned

00:02:00.530 --> 00:02:02.810
or operated businesses remain registered

00:02:02.810 --> 00:02:05.150
with the Greenwood Chamber of Commerce.

00:02:05.150 --> 00:02:07.230
- The Historic Greenwood
Chamber of Commerce

00:02:07.230 --> 00:02:10.593
owns the last 10 buildings
known as Black Wall Street.

00:02:11.920 --> 00:02:14.310
We house 33 businesses.

00:02:14.310 --> 00:02:16.560
31 of them are African American.

00:02:16.560 --> 00:02:20.150
So we're still doing
what our ancestors did.

00:02:20.150 --> 00:02:21.790
It might not be Black Wall Street,

00:02:21.790 --> 00:02:24.070
but it's definitely a Black Main Street.

00:02:24.070 --> 00:02:27.060
And so we have to preserve this.

00:02:27.060 --> 00:02:28.230
- [Narrator] While
there's a growing number

00:02:28.230 --> 00:02:30.670
of Black-owned businesses
in this district,

00:02:30.670 --> 00:02:32.910
some of the newer
establishments are tenants

00:02:32.910 --> 00:02:35.130
in buildings owned by white developers.

00:02:35.130 --> 00:02:38.010
That's a reversal of
fortune from 100 years ago

00:02:38.010 --> 00:02:40.970
when many of the property
owners were Black.

00:02:40.970 --> 00:02:43.320
The massacre destroyed real estate assets

00:02:43.320 --> 00:02:46.033
that could have been passed
to future generations.

00:02:48.540 --> 00:02:51.850
- Our oldest living survivor, Daddy Clark,

00:02:51.850 --> 00:02:54.330
died at 109 years old.

00:02:54.330 --> 00:02:55.350
He was a teenager.

00:02:55.350 --> 00:02:58.750
His photograph is on
exhibit in the gallery

00:02:58.750 --> 00:03:00.960
- [Narrator] Tulsa residents
like Mechelle Brown-Burdex,

00:03:00.960 --> 00:03:03.160
say it's important to
keep telling the story

00:03:03.160 --> 00:03:06.030
of how prosperous Black
residents of Greenwood were

00:03:06.030 --> 00:03:07.400
before it's decline.

00:03:07.400 --> 00:03:10.380
- We were never taught
that African-Americans

00:03:10.380 --> 00:03:12.070
were business owners,

00:03:12.070 --> 00:03:13.340
that they were pilots,

00:03:13.340 --> 00:03:16.680
and electricians, and
doctors, and attorneys.

00:03:16.680 --> 00:03:21.423
And I was shocked that we
had never learned about this.

00:03:22.670 --> 00:03:25.470
Being born in Tulsa,
being raised in Tulsa,

00:03:25.470 --> 00:03:28.820
attending Black history classes.

00:03:28.820 --> 00:03:31.350
- [Narrator] Brown-Burdex
coordinates educational programs

00:03:31.350 --> 00:03:34.070
and tours for the
Greenwood Cultural Center.

00:03:34.070 --> 00:03:36.470
- We thought that this
was the perfect time

00:03:36.470 --> 00:03:39.160
in the spirit of Black Wall Street

00:03:39.160 --> 00:03:43.690
to identify and promote
Black-owned businesses

00:03:43.690 --> 00:03:45.300
in our community.

00:03:45.300 --> 00:03:46.420
- [Narrator] As the city commemorates

00:03:46.420 --> 00:03:48.220
the centennial of the massacre,

00:03:48.220 --> 00:03:51.290
Brown-Burdex has teamed up
with a local co-working space

00:03:51.290 --> 00:03:53.150
and incubator to create a guide

00:03:53.150 --> 00:03:55.850
of Black-owned businesses in the area.

00:03:55.850 --> 00:03:58.090
- When we first began this work,

00:03:58.090 --> 00:04:01.330
many people were opposed to us

00:04:01.330 --> 00:04:04.490
even acknowledging or
recognizing the history

00:04:04.490 --> 00:04:07.530
of Black Wall Street or of the massacre.

00:04:07.530 --> 00:04:10.070
Now, as we approach the commemoration,

00:04:10.070 --> 00:04:11.763
there is much more support.

00:04:13.060 --> 00:04:14.610
- [Narrator] It's clear
things are changing again

00:04:14.610 --> 00:04:16.160
in the Greenwood neighborhood.

00:04:16.160 --> 00:04:18.730
A different museum called Greenwood Rising

00:04:18.730 --> 00:04:20.400
is among the construction projects

00:04:20.400 --> 00:04:22.263
redefining the look of the area.

00:04:24.010 --> 00:04:28.970
- It's a challenge because some
of our work is quite similar

00:04:28.970 --> 00:04:33.970
but we are finding ways that
we can compliment one another

00:04:35.220 --> 00:04:38.280
as opposed to competing with one another.

00:04:38.280 --> 00:04:40.370
- [Narrator] Oklahoma State
Senator Kevin Matthews,

00:04:40.370 --> 00:04:42.960
who heads the commission
overseeing Greenwood Rising,

00:04:42.960 --> 00:04:45.320
says the museum is
working with organizations

00:04:45.320 --> 00:04:46.700
throughout the Historic District

00:04:46.700 --> 00:04:49.323
to tell the neighborhood
story in cooperative ways.

00:04:50.530 --> 00:04:53.370
Still, Brown-Burdex says
her vision for Greenwood

00:04:53.370 --> 00:04:54.840
remains the same.

00:04:54.840 --> 00:04:58.160
- Personally, I would love to see more

00:04:58.160 --> 00:05:00.990
Black-owned businesses in
the Greenwood district.

00:05:00.990 --> 00:05:05.990
I would love to see home
ownership increase in this area.

00:05:09.200 --> 00:05:11.280
- [Narrator] After being displaced
by urban renewal projects

00:05:11.280 --> 00:05:13.370
decades ago, many Black Tulsans

00:05:13.370 --> 00:05:15.691
now live in the city's north side.

00:05:15.691 --> 00:05:16.572
- Mm-hm.

00:05:16.572 --> 00:05:20.822
This is my home, this is
neighborhood I grew up in.

00:05:22.720 --> 00:05:25.690
- [Narrator] Tyrance Billingsley
II, a tech entrepreneur,

00:05:25.690 --> 00:05:27.820
recently learned about his family's ties

00:05:27.820 --> 00:05:30.830
to the rebirth of Greenwood in the 1930s.

00:05:30.830 --> 00:05:33.370
- What I know is little,
but I do know that

00:05:33.370 --> 00:05:36.470
my direct descendants
were cousins of people

00:05:36.470 --> 00:05:38.810
who helped donate to Vernon A.M.E. Church

00:05:38.810 --> 00:05:40.190
and help rebuild it.

00:05:40.190 --> 00:05:41.990
- [Narrator] Billingsley
is now looking to carry on

00:05:41.990 --> 00:05:44.053
the spirit of Greenwood in his own way.

00:05:44.990 --> 00:05:47.210
- The actual district of Greenwood,

00:05:47.210 --> 00:05:49.683
obviously it's being heavily gentrified.

00:05:50.610 --> 00:05:53.010
I like to think of Greenwood
as two different things.

00:05:53.010 --> 00:05:55.840
The body is the land in and of itself.

00:05:55.840 --> 00:05:58.220
And then there's the
spirit, or the breath.

00:05:58.220 --> 00:06:00.180
The breath of Greenwood is the spirit

00:06:00.180 --> 00:06:01.821
that Black entrepreneurship,

00:06:01.821 --> 00:06:03.320
the sense of community,

00:06:03.320 --> 00:06:05.770
the breath of Greenwood
is very much still alive.

00:06:06.680 --> 00:06:08.300
- [Narrator] Billingsley
is spearheading a project

00:06:08.300 --> 00:06:11.200
he hopes will bring opportunities
for today's Black Tulsans

00:06:11.200 --> 00:06:12.890
to create the kind of generational wealth

00:06:12.890 --> 00:06:15.560
seen decades ago on Black Wall Street.

00:06:15.560 --> 00:06:17.120
- Block Tech Street is an initiative

00:06:17.120 --> 00:06:20.670
to rebirth Black Wall Street
as the premier Black tech hub

00:06:20.670 --> 00:06:21.940
here in Tulsa.

00:06:21.940 --> 00:06:23.770
- [Narrator] Currently
in its beginning stages,

00:06:23.770 --> 00:06:26.270
one aim of the project is to weave coding

00:06:26.270 --> 00:06:29.280
and other applicable skills
into afterschool programs

00:06:29.280 --> 00:06:30.860
for Black children.

00:06:30.860 --> 00:06:33.320
Billingsley says he has about $1 million

00:06:33.320 --> 00:06:34.500
in verbal commitments,

00:06:34.500 --> 00:06:37.100
and is working with partners to fundraise.

00:06:37.100 --> 00:06:39.350
- We have a goal of
facilitating $1 billion

00:06:39.350 --> 00:06:40.840
worth of investment in this community

00:06:40.840 --> 00:06:42.490
over the next 10 years,

00:06:42.490 --> 00:06:45.090
you know, around six strategic pillars.

00:06:45.090 --> 00:06:48.130
Entrepreneur support,
narrative and communications,

00:06:48.130 --> 00:06:51.163
capital, workforce,
infrastructure, and policy.

00:06:53.100 --> 00:06:55.250
- [Narrator] Other Black
entrepreneurs are interested in

00:06:55.250 --> 00:06:57.160
rebuilding wealth in this area,

00:06:57.160 --> 00:07:00.070
but some Black Tulsans say
the city must do a better job

00:07:00.070 --> 00:07:01.900
in reconciling with its past

00:07:01.900 --> 00:07:05.163
to protect the area's Black
institutions and businesses.

00:07:06.140 --> 00:07:09.650
- I want it to be so that
an endowment is set up

00:07:09.650 --> 00:07:11.940
so that these buildings are maintained,

00:07:11.940 --> 00:07:14.703
and that economic
development can be fostered.

00:07:16.440 --> 00:07:21.040
- Hopefully, undoubtedly,
we will have a conversation.

00:07:21.040 --> 00:07:25.223
We will see some type of
real reparations take place.

00:07:26.110 --> 00:07:30.070
Black Wall Street as it was in 1921,

00:07:30.070 --> 00:07:34.090
prior to the massacre and,
as it was once it was rebuilt

00:07:34.090 --> 00:07:38.210
in the 30s and 40s and
50s may never be again.

00:07:38.210 --> 00:07:41.700
But Black Wall Street is an idea.

00:07:41.700 --> 00:07:45.740
I appreciate the businesses that are here

00:07:45.740 --> 00:07:47.120
in the Greenwood District.

00:07:47.120 --> 00:07:49.600
And then we have the
Greenwood Cultural Center.

00:07:49.600 --> 00:07:53.030
We remain here telling the story.

00:07:53.030 --> 00:07:57.184
We are actually looking
forward to the next 100 years.

00:07:57.184 --> 00:08:00.017
(emotional music)

